# Frontend quality

Applies to the React + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind + shadcn/ui frontend, including the react-three-fiber globe.

## TypeScript

- **`strict` mode on.** No `any` (use `unknown` + narrowing, or proper types). No non-null assertions (`!`) to silence the checker—handle the null case.
- Types for API payloads come from the **generated types** in `frontend/src/types/` (`canonical-event-schema.mdc`); do not hand-redeclare event shapes.
- `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit` and `pnpm lint` (eslint) must pass; do not disable lint rules inline without justification.

## Hygiene

- **No committed `console.log`/`debugger`** (use a logger or remove). No commented-out dead code.
- No hardcoded secrets or API base URLs—use env (`import.meta.env`).
- Keep components focused; colocate hooks; follow the existing structure.

## Theming (command-center aesthetic)

- Use **theme tokens** (Tailwind config / CSS variables for the amber-on-near-black palette) instead of hardcoded hex colors. The blurred/transparent sidebars use the shared backdrop-blur utilities, not ad-hoc styles.
- Desktop-first, dark theme; build with i18next so strings are translatable (no hardcoded user-facing copy where i18n is expected).

## react-three-fiber / globe performance (perf-critical surface)

- **Dispose** geometries, materials, and textures you create; avoid leaks across re-renders.
- **Memoize** expensive objects (geometries, shader materials) and avoid recreating them every frame/render; keep heavy work out of the render loop.
- **Instance** markers (instanced meshes / points) when rendering many events instead of one mesh per event; cluster at low zoom.
- Do per-frame work in `useFrame` sparingly; avoid setState in the render loop. Drive large data via buffers/attributes, not React state per point.
- Load event data by **viewport (bbox) + filters** from the API (`geospatial-postgis.mdc`)—do not fetch the whole dataset to the client.

## Before "done"

- `pnpm lint`, `tsc --noEmit`, `pnpm build` pass; Playwright smoke of changed view (`regression-testing.mdc`); globe stays responsive with realistic event counts.
